<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pemayangtse Monastery</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pemayangtse Monastery is a Buddhist monastery of the Nyingma school near Pelling in western Sikkim, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, founded in the late 17th or early 18th century. It was one of the leading monasteries of the kingdom of Sikkim, whose monks were traditionally drawn from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhutia">Bhutia</a> families of high standing and performed rites for the royal court. It stands on a ridge near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabdentse">Rabdentse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pemayangtse-monastery.jpg" alt="Pemayangtse Monastery" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kothanda Srinivasan · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Main_Shrine_of_Pemangytse_Gompa_with_prayer_flags.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
